+# Tasks: S005 Delivery status
+
+**Input**: `spec.md` and `plan.md` in this directory.
+
+**Prerequisites**: The supplied corpus contains no application source, test manifest, contracts, data model, or epic breakdown. These tasks use the reversible repository convention `src/`, `migrations/`, and `tests/`; the implementer must translate paths to the established project layout if it has since been added, without changing the stated behavior.
+
+## Implementation context
+
+### Requirement → task mapping
+
+| Requirement | Implementing tasks | Test coverage |
+|---|---|---|
+| FR-001 — authenticate each provider callback, deduplicate by provider event ID, persist its delivery status under `workspace_id`, and expose `GET /actions/{id}/delivery` only to the owning workspace | Tasks 4–10 | Tasks 1–3, 11–12 |
+
+**Coverage check**: FR-001 maps to implementation and failure-path work. Task 13 is the explicit verification gate for the complete checklist.
+
+### Locked implementation decisions from `plan.md`
+
+1. `delivery_events` is the durable idempotency record. Its uniqueness is scoped to the provider event identifier and workspace, so a replay cannot create a second status event.
+2. The callback path verifies the provider signature before any database mutation. Invalid or missing signatures are rejected without persistence.
+3. Both persistence and reads carry `workspace_id`; the GET route authorizes using the real request-role workspace context, never a bypass role or mocked policy.
+
+### Parallel safety
+
+`[P]` appears only on independent test files. Migration work, callback service work, and routes are sequential because they share the delivery event contract and request behavior.
+
+### Phase 1: Contract and failing integration probes
+
+- [ ] T001 [P] Write the failing callback contract tests for `POST /callbacks/reminder` in `tests/contract/reminder-callback.test.ts`.
+
+  **Implements**: FR-001 callback authentication and provider-event deduplication.
+
+  **Pattern**: Send a correctly signed callback and assert the accepted response shape; send a missing, malformed, and invalid signature and assert rejection with no success payload.
+
+  **Acceptance predicate**: Before the callback and read routes exist, valid callback behavior is red and every invalid-signature case is red.
+
+  **Test command**: `npm test -- tests/contract/reminder-callback.test.ts`
+
+  **File**: `tests/contract/reminder-callback.test.ts`
+
